1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Subtitles added by Hanson Hu

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Episode 18 - Making a Difference

3
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,200
I don't believe it!

4
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:55,340
What's wrong?

5
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:57,160
Carter Boswell!

6
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,020
Who's Carter Boswell?

7
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,880
He's running for the school board.

8
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,120
The election's next month.

9
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,180
What's wrong with wanting to be on the school board?

10
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:05,560
Nothing.

11
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,920
But he wants to cut the school budget!

12
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,860
Maybe it needs cutting.

13
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,320
Cutting the budget is fine,

14
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,320
but he wants to do it

15
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,080
by cutting all the cultural programs.

16
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:17,720
No music, no dance,

17
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,000
no concert, no stage presentations.

18
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,240
Why does he want to do that?

19
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,540
He says it's to save the taxpayers' money,

20
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:26,440
and I think he believes

21
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,040
that the taxpayers will vote for him

22
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,840
if he spends less on the cultural programs.

23
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,640
He's probably right.

24
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,480
Lots of people want their taxes

25
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,020
used for new books

26
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,840
and a new paint job in the schoolrooms.

27
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:41,680
Maybe some of us would like to pay a little bit more

28
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:44,040
and keep the cultural programs for our kids.

29
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:46,440
Well, I'm not sure, Ellen.

30
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,300
I hear it from my patients.

31
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:52,480
Lots of people are tired of higher taxes.

32
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,000
I know,

33
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,700
but if Boswell wins

34
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:00,220
he'll be an important decision-maker

35
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:01,360
on the school board,

36
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,360
and he doesn't know anything

37
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,100
about our children's education.

38
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,500
Who's running against him?

39
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:08,320
Nobody. That's the problem.

40
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,720
Well, it sounds to me like Carter Boswell

41
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,600
is going to win this seat on the board.

42
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,440
Oh, not if I can stop him!

43
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:18,360
And how are you going to stop him?

44
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,280
I don't know.

45
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,700
Maybe I'll run against him.

46
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:28,360
Well, you've got my vote.

47
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,460
I'm serious, Philip.

48
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,340
Why shouldn't I run?

49
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,120
Why shouldn't you run for what, Mom?

50
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,400
Your mother is thinking of

51
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,640
running for the school board.

52
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,720
Hey, that's terrific, Mom!

53
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,400
Against Carter Boswell?

54
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:46,360
Great!

55
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:48,600
Well, if I run for office,

56
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,220
the voters will have a clear choice.

57
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,740
I stand for everything Boswell doesn't.

58
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:56,320
I think a lot of people will vote for you

59
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,500
against Boswell, Ellen.

60
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,280
I'll vote for you.

61
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:02,080
Will you help me if I do run?

62
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,320
Absolutely.

63
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:05,580
The trouble is

64
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,140
it takes a little bit of money to run a campaign.

65
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:11,160
I think you can make a difference, Ellen.

66
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,000
And in a short campaign

67
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:14,280
you wouldn't need as much money.

68
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,860
You know something, Ellen?

69
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:19,700
Why not give the people of Riverdale a clear choice?

70
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,120
I'm with you.

71
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,180
You can make a difference.

72
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,220
Come in.

73
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:36,240
Mr. Maxwell?

74
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,160
Yes, Charles Maxwell.

75
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,380
My name is Ellen Stewart.

76
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,600
Hello.

77
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,960
Please, sit down.

78
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,880
You asked to see me.

79
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,000
What would you like to see me about?

80
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,100
I'd like your help.

81
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:01,920
Well, I'm editor of the most influential newspaper in Riverdale.

82
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:04,900
Actually, it's the only newspaper.

83
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:07,800
A lot of people would like my help.

84
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,620
Do you have a story?

85
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,940
I'm planning to run for the school board.

86
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,240
Against Carter Boswell?

87
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,000
Yes.

88
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,680
Well, that is news.

89
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,700
Will you announce that I'm running?

90
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,760
Sure.

91
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,760
But I need some information.

92
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,160
Of course.

93
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:29,880
Why will the voters vote for you against Boswell,

94
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:30,280
Mrs. Stewart?

95
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,020
Because I care.

96
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:38,600
"Vote for Ellen Stewart. She cares."

97
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,220
Not a bad slogan.

98
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,160
But what do you care about?

99
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,900
Well, I care about the children of our town.

100
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,900
I don't want them to grow up

101
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:51,480
without cultural programs in our school.

102
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,600
Do you have a plan?

103
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:57,360
I want our children to learn

104
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,760
more than reading, writing, and arithmetic.

105
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,560
I want to keep the after-school programs -

106
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,760
the music, the concerts.

107
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,440
It's not a bad plan.

108
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:10,400
But who's going to pay for all of this?

109
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:11,600
We are.

110
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:13,620
The citizens of Riverdale, of course.

111
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:14,960
I plan to get help

112
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,380
from the businessmen and the corporations of Riverdale.

113
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,560
That's fair enough.

114
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,560
Exactly what do you want from me, Mrs. Stewart?

115
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,480
You don't know me.

116
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:30,540
I can't expect you to take my side against Boswell.

117
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:32,840
But I do need some publicity

118
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,360
so that the people of our town

119
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:36,040
know that I'm running for office

120
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,580
and that I care about our children.

121
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,240
Fair enough.

122
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,920
I certainly can print the news.

123
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,240
And you are now making news.

124
00:06:56,880 --> 00:07:02,180
Why will the voters vote for you against Boswell, Mrs. Stewart?

125
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,760
Because I care.

126
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:10,060
"Vote for Ellen Stewart. She cares."

127
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,920
Not a bad slogan.

128
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,840
"Ellen Stewart. She cares."

129
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:19,520
It is a good campaign slogan.

130
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:23,140
People will hear it and know what I stand for.

131
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,680
I care.

132
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:27,980
I care about our children's education,

133
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:33,480
not just the school buildings themselves, but the children.

134
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:39,840
I care about what children study and what they learn.

135
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,440
I want them to learn about a variety of subjects,

136
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:45,160
including music and literature and art.

137
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:49,320
And I care about our children's activities after school.

138
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,740
I want to keep their music programs,

139
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:59,920
like the orchestra and the chorus.

140
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:04,220
I want children to experience the joys of music.

141
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,000
I play the piano myself,

142
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:10,120
and I've taught music to many children in Riverdale.

143
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:13,300
I want to keep the other after-school programs, too.

144
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,500
I have a plan.

145
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:24,280
I'll get local businesses, banks

146
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,800
and other companies in the community to help.

147
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:29,740
We all have children in this town,

148
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:33,040
and I believe that parents care about education.

149
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:36,180
And I want to be on the Riverdale School Board.

150
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,600
I know it's a big responsibility,

151
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,640
but I know I can make a difference,

152
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,100
because I care.

153
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:30,700
Here are the fliers, hot off the press!

154
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,800
Looks good.

155
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:37,840
Simple.

156
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Right over here, Grandpa.

157
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,860
You fold the fliers.

158
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,940
Richard and I will put them into the envelopes.

159
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:46,800
We finished addressing over three hundred envelopes.

160
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,680
Need another box?

161
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:49,760
Good work, gang.

162
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,060
Hi, this is Mike Johnson.

163
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,880
Can I speak with Mr. or Mrs. Anderson?

164
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:53,960
Mr. Nelson.

165
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,040
Hi. This is Robbie Stewart.

166
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:56,920
Did you know

167
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,480
my mother is running for the school board?

168
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,180
Yes, Miss Kim, Ellen Stewart.

169
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:01,020
"She cares."

170
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,320
Oh, see you at the polls.

171
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:04,280
Certainly.

172
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,720
I'll give her your best wishes,

173
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,280
Mr. Nelson.

174
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,320
Hi, this is Mike Johnson.

175
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,140
Can I speak with Mr. or Mrs. Burns?

176
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,300
Thank you.

177
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:11,640
We have done so much

178
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,920
in such a short amount of time.

179
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,640
I can't believe it!

180
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:16,700
Wait till Philip comes home and sees our progress.

181
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:19,460
Everyone saw the story in the Riverdale newspaper.

182
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:21,480
Mr. Maxwell was very kind

183
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,520
to print my announcement.

184
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,920
It helps enormously.

185
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,960
Everybody in Riverdale reads his paper.

186
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:30,140
Your photo in it helped, too.

187
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:32,180
Thanks to you, Richard,

188
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:33,520
it's a good picture.

189
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:35,300
Well, hi, all.

190
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:35,700
Hi, Dad.

191
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:36,520
Hello, darling.

192
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:38,340
May I... may I help?

193
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,760
Licking envelopes.

194
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:42,260
I fold the fliers.

195
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:43,320
We stuff them.

196
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:46,760
And I lick the envelopes.

197
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,680
Hey, everybody,

198
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,440
Mrs. Greenberg is on the phone.

199
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:54,240
She says Carter Boswell is on the TV right now -

200
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,460
doing a commercial.

201
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:56,600
What channel?

202
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,280
Five.

203
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,240
Five?

204
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:06,600
And if you ask what I care about, I'll tell you.

205
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:10,920
I care about the school buildings in need of paint.

206
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,680
I care about more lockers for the teachers.

207
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:17,960
I care about new fixtures in the hallways,

208
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:21,600
not music or dancing or entertainment.

209
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,860
I care about the practical things.

210
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:28,960
If you do, vote for me, Carter Boswell.

211
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:34,120
A lot of people will agree with him.

212
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,360
I told you.

213
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,460
Too bad kids can't vote.

214
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,760
It's our school, but we can't vote.

215
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
There are people in favor of the cultural programs, Mom.

216
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,480
There are, Ellen.

217
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:51,560
Don't be upset by Boswell's commercial.

218
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:54,160
You have to go on television, too.

219
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:57,800
Boswell's a powerful speaker.

220
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,820
You can be, too.

221
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,600
Your ideas are good ones.

222
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,740
I don't know.

223
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:12,380
I'm not sure I'm up to it.

224
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,200
Vote! Vote! Vote! Vote! Vote! Vote!

225
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:33,080
Hey, everybody, here's what we say.

226
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:35,520
Get out and vote on election day.

227
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:38,100
You can make a difference, it's up to you.

228
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,720
We need your vote if you want better schools.

229
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,920
So clap your hands.

230
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,480
Stomp your feet.

231
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:48,420
Ellen Stewart's running for the school board,

232
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:50,780
and we know she can't be beat.

233
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:53,400
I said clap your hands,

234
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,880
and stomp your feet.

235
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:58,800
Ellen Stewart's running for the school board,

236
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:01,200
and we know she can't be beat.

237
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:04,000
So vote! Vote! Vote!

238
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,720
If you want better schools,

239
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,200
and if you want your vote to count,

240
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,920
Ellen Stewart is the one to choose.

241
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,280
Who do we want?

242
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,840
Ellen Stewart!

243
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,080
Who's gonna win?

244
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:17,280
Ellen Stewart!

245
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:18,880
Who do we want?

246
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,040
Ellen Stewart!

247
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,200
Who's gonna win?

248
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,400
Ellen Stewart!

249
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,880
Hey! What do you say?

250
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,360
Ellen Stewart!

251
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,480
All the way!

252
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:31,320
Hey! Come on, let's fight for Ellen Stewart.

253
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,640
She's the one who's right.

254
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:35,320
So everybody just be aware

255
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:37,880
that Ellen Stewart is the one who cares.

256
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:40,480
She'll make a difference for everyone,

257
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:44,140
'cause Ellen Stewart is number one.

258
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:48,560
She knows the importance of music and art.

259
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:51,220
Cultural programs play a big part.

260
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,640
Let's keep these programs in our schools.

261
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:56,020
Ellen Stewart's for me and you.

262
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,960
So let's all give her a cheer.

263
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:01,320
Everything's all right 'cause Ellen's here.

264
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:02,600
Who do we want?

265
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,080
Ellen Stewart!

266
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,280
Who do we want?

267
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,540
Ellen Stewart!

268
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:07,360
I say yeah!

269
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:09,160
Yeah! We vote for Ellen!

270
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:10,500
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

271
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,740
We're yelling for Ellen!

272
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,840
Yeah! Yeah!

273
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,660
We're yelling for Ellen!

274
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:18,660
Yeah!

275
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:02,780
My slogan is "I care".

276
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:07,480
I care about people, not things.

277
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:10,480
Vote for me, Ellen Stewart.

278
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:13,600
I care.

279
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,000
How was it?

280
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,100
You were terrific!

281
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:26,800
Can I see it?

282
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:27,380
Sure.

283
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:36,540
Hello. My name is Ellen Stewart,

284
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,760
and I'm running for the open seat on the school board.

285
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:43,560
My slogan is "I care".

286
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,260
What does the word care mean?

287
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:50,960
I care about people, not things.

288
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,920
Vote for me, Ellen Stewart.

289
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,200
I care.

290
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:01,400
I like it,

291
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:02,980
but now what?

292
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:06,720
How can we possibly get it on so Riverdale

293
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:08,440
will see it and hear it?

294
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,520
Leave it to me.

295
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,880
I mean that when I say "I care",

296
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:22,480
I care about people, not things.

297
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:26,440
Vote for me, Ellen Stewart.

298
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,160
I care.

299
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,860
What happened?

300
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,960
Mom is now on television

301
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,840
in every appliance store in Riverdale,

302
00:16:36,940 --> 00:16:38,000
except Hamlin's.

303
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,160
He's a Boswell voter.

304
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,400
That's a brilliant idea, Richard!

305
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,740
You inherited your father's brains.

306
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,080
We got our brains from you, Dad.

307
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,220
And guess what?

308
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,840
I called channel five.

309
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,800
Their TV news is going to cover it.

310
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:55,180
"Housewife campaigns in appliance stores."

311
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:56,020
And I'll bet

312
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:58,040
some magazine will pick up the story, too.

313
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:59,720
Mom, you're going to win!

314
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:00,560
I know it!

315
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,880
Hold it, Robbie!

316
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,280
Just cool down.

317
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,560
I know we're getting some attention now,

318
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:09,260
but in the end the voters will have to decide.

319
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:12,000
You're gonna win.

320
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:13,080
Trust me!

321
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:18,180
In the hotly contested race

322
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:20,560
for the one seat on the Riverdale School Board,

323
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,600
Mrs. Ellen Stewart has taken an early lead.

324
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,000
She's winning!

325
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:26,460
{\an8}[TV Reporter] Now returning to other local news...

326
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:26,460
Mom, you're winning!

327
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:27,600
{\an8}[TV Reporter] Riverdale High School

328
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,680
{\an8}[TV Reporter] beat its rival Horace Mann in baseball today.

329
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,320
It's too soon to know for certain.

330
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:30,680
You're ahead.

331
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:31,940
That's better than being behind.

332
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:31,940
{\an8}[TV Reporter] More sports after this.

333
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:33,560
It's not over yet.

334
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,580
Let's just all calm down,

335
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:37,320
and wait for the final results.

336
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:41,040
Ellen, why don't you go out to the backyard

337
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:42,480
and get some fresh air?

338
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,340
Thank you, Grandpa.

339
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,460
I need some.

340
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:08,500
What happened?

341
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,360
You came very close, Ellen.

342
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:19,440
You lost by only a hundred and twenty-one votes.

343
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,540
I lost.

344
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:30,760
You tried, Mom.

345
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:33,680
You lost by a very small number of votes.

346
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:37,200
Only one hundred and twenty-one votes!

347
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:39,720
I'm sorry, Mom.

348
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,420
There just wasn't enough time.

349
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,060
Look, you've made a very strong impression

350
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,300
on our community.

351
00:18:48,420 --> 00:18:51,080
You'll have another chance next election.

352
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,260
Hello.

353
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:04,520
Oh, yes, yes, Mr. Maxwell.

354
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:16,280
Hello, Mr. Maxwell.

355
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,800
How are you?

356
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,040
I just called to tell you

357
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,200
that you are very impressive.

358
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,720
You lost the election,

359
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:25,120
but you won the attention of the residents of Riverdale,

360
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,380
of Boswell, and of me.

361
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:31,080
Well, thank you, Mr. Maxwell.

362
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,980
I appreciate your kind words.

363
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:34,420
I needed that.

364
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:36,520
I hear Boswell

365
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:38,600
wants to appoint you to a special arts committee.

366
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:40,480
I'm sending over a reporter

367
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:42,000
in the morning to interview you.

368
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,120
You are?

369
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:46,360
I'm going to do an article

370
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:48,840
on "Ellen Stewart, she cares".

371
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,260
Maybe we'll all care now.

372
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,440
Good-bye.

373
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:56,840
Thank you,

374
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:58,900
and good-bye.

375
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:06,880
What was that about?

376
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:09,040
You were right, Philip.

377
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,080
I did make a difference in town.

378
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,960
And in this family.

379
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,640
Good evening.

380
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:33,820
An important local election took place today in Riverdale.

381
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:38,000
The people of this community elected a new member of the school board,

382
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,200
Carter Boswell.

383
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:44,040
Opposing him in the campaign was Ellen Stewart, a housewife from Riverdale.

384
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:47,280
Tonight, we'll take a look at both campaigns.

385
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:50,120
First, we turn to the Boswell campaign.

386
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:54,200
Mr. Boswell reached many voters by appearing on local TV.

387
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:57,880
I care about the school buildings in need of paint.

388
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:00,840
I care about more lockers for the teachers.

389
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:04,800
I care about new fixtures in the hallways.

390
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:08,600
Less than a month ago, a new face entered the race.

391
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,640
Ellen Stewart.

392
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:14,500
Mrs. Stewart disagreed with Carter Boswell's plans for the Riverdale schools.

393
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:18,360
She campaigned very strongly to keep the cultural programs

394
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,240
in music, art and drama.

395
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:22,920
Local appliance stores played a videotape

396
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:25,540
of Mrs. Stewart introducing herself to the voters.

397
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:28,040
My name is Ellen Stewart,

398
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:31,320
and I'm running for the open seat on the school board.

399
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,920
My slogan is "I care".

400
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:38,200
I care about people, not things.

401
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:43,400
Mrs. Stewart's unusual campaign helped her win the attention of the local newspaper.

402
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:46,480
Charles Maxwell, the editor of the Riverdale News,

403
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:51,060
praised Mrs. Stewart for caring about the cultural programs in the schools.

404
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:53,880
When the first votes were counted early in the day,

405
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:58,480
it seemed as if Ellen Stewart might win a surprise victory over Carter Boswell.

406
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:00,560
But once all the votes were counted,

407
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:02,660
Mrs. Stewart lost by only a hundred and twenty-one votes.

408
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,820
Well, it was a very close election,

409
00:22:07,020 --> 00:22:10,480
and Ellen Stewart convinced the people of Riverdale that she cared.

410
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:12,640
She also convinced Carter Boswell,

411
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:15,000
who now wants to appoint Mrs. Stewart

412
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,480
to a special committee for cultural programs in the schools.

413
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:21,220
Well, that's our special Election Day report

414
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:23,400
on a very important local election.

415
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,620
Thank you, and have a good evening.

